(24, 1, '2017-10-20 14:52:27', '2017-10-20 09:22:27', '<h1><img class=\"wp-image-26 alignright\" src=\"http://techwinky.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/10/IMG_20170219_110354-e1508489263874.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"183\" height=\"184\" />My Story:-</h1>\n<h5>Hi! I am Sanjit Chakrabarti. I am doing Btech in computer engineering, graduating in 2019.</h5>\n<h5>After learning to code in my second semester, I started using only Linux in 2016. I started with Ubuntu first, as usual. I then finished reading this Book \'<a href=\"http://linuxcommand.org/tlcl.php\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">The Linux Command Line</a>\' and did a course on Linux administration in Udemy (LINK:- <a href=\"https://www.udemy.com/linux-administration/learn/v4/\">https://www.udemy.com/linux-administration/learn/v4/</a> ).</h5>\n<h5>Then after tinkering with Ubuntu for months, I installed Arch Linux on my PC to get more control over my OS. I am now a happy user of Arch Linux.</h5>\n<h5>In 2018, I did GSoC and successfully completed it too. Now, my main aim is to become a Web developer, specializing in React.</h5>\n<h5>So, I opened this blog to share some great tips and tutorials related to web development.</h5>\n<h5>In free time, I like to cycle far away places and love to volunteer in an NGO.</h5>\n<h5></h5>\n<h5>Follow me on:-</h5>\n<h5>Twitter - <a href=\"https://twitter.com/sujitsanjit?lang=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">@sujitsanjit</a></h5>\n<h5>Linkedin - <a href=\"http://www.linkedin.com/in/sanjit-chakrabarti-pro\">sanjit-chakrabarti-pro</a></h5>\n<h5>Check out my work -  <a href=\"https://github.com/sanjitchak\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">sanjitchak</a></h5>', 'About Me', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'about-me', '', '', '2019-03-04 16:42:45', '2019-03-04 11:12:45', '', 0, 'http://techwinky.com/?page_id=24', 0, 'page', '', 0),
(26, 1, '2017-10-20 14:15:44', '2017-10-20 08:45:44', '', 'IMG_20170219_110354', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'closed', '', 'img_20170219_110354', '', '', '2017-10-20 14:15:44', '2017-10-20 08:45:44', '', 24, 'http://techwinky.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/10/IMG_20170219_110354.jpg', 0, 'attachment', 'image/jpeg', 0),
(27, 1, '2017-10-20 14:17:07', '2017-10-20 08:47:07', '<img class=\"alignleft wp-image-26 size-full\" src=\"http://techwinky.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/10/IMG_20170219_110354-e1508489213489.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"732\" height=\"724\" />\r\n\r\nHi! I am Sanjit Chakrabarti. I am doing Btech in computer engineering, graduating in 2019.\r\n\r\nAfter learning to code in my second semester, I started using Linux and ditched windows forever in 2016. I started with Ubuntu first, as usual. I then finished reading a book about \'Linux command Line\' (LINK:- http://linuxcommand.org/tlcl.php ) and did a course on Linux administration in Udemy (LINK:- <a href=\"https://www.udemy.com/linux-administration/learn/v4/\">https://www.udemy.com/linux-administration/learn/v4/</a> ).\r\n\r\nThen after tinkering with Ubuntu for months, I installed Arch Linux on my PC. I now am a happy user of Arch Linux for months now. So, I opened this blog to share some great tips and tutorials on Arch Linux.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;', 'About Me', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '24-revision-v1', '', '', '2017-10-20 14:17:07', '2017-10-20 08:47:07', '', 24, 'http://techwinky.com/24-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(28, 1, '2017-10-20 14:19:55', '2017-10-20 08:49:55', '<img class=\"wp-image-26  alignright\" src=\"http://techwinky.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/10/IMG_20170219_110354-e1508489263874.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"183\" height=\"184\" />Hi! I am Sanjit Chakrabarti. I am doing Btech in computer engineering, graduating in 2019.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\nAfter learning to code in my second semester, I started using only Linux in 2016. I started with Ubuntu first, as usual. I then finished reading a book about \'Linux command Line\' (LINK:- http://linuxcommand.org/tlcl.php ) and did a course on Linux administration in Udemy (LINK:- <a href=\"https://www.udemy.com/linux-administration/learn/v4/\">https://www.udemy.com/linux-administration/learn/v4/</a> ).\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\nThen after tinkering with Ubuntu for months, I installed Arch Linux on my PC. I am now a happy user of Arch Linux for months now. So, I opened this blog to share some great tips and tutorials on Arch Linux.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;', 'About Me', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '24-revision-v1', '', '', '2017-10-20 14:19:55', '2017-10-20 08:49:55', '', 24, 'http://techwinky.com/24-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(29, 1, '2017-10-20 14:24:17', '2017-10-20 08:54:17', '<img class=\"wp-image-26  alignright\" src=\"http://techwinky.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/10/IMG_20170219_110354-e1508489263874.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"183\" height=\"184\" />Hi! I am Sanjit Chakrabarti. I am doing Btech in computer engineering, graduating in 2019.\r\n\r\nAfter learning to code in my second semester, I started using only Linux in 2016. I started with Ubuntu first, as usual. I then finished reading a book about \'Linux command Line\' (LINK:- http://linuxcommand.org/tlcl.php ) and did a course on Linux administration in Udemy (LINK:- <a href=\"https://www.udemy.com/linux-administration/learn/v4/\">https://www.udemy.com/linux-administration/learn/v4/</a> ).\r\n\r\nThen after tinkering with Ubuntu for months, I installed Arch Linux on my PC. I am now a happy user of Arch Linux for months now. So, I opened this blog to share some great tips and tutorials on Arch Linux.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;', 'About Me', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '24-revision-v1', '', '', '2017-10-20 14:24:17', '2017-10-20 08:54:17', '', 24, 'http://techwinky.com/24-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(30, 1, '2017-10-20 14:52:12', '2017-10-20 09:22:12', '<img class=\"wp-image-26  alignright\" src=\"http://techwinky.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/10/IMG_20170219_110354-e1508489263874.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"183\" height=\"184\" />Hi! I am Sanjit Chakrabarti. I am doing Btech in computer engineering, graduating in 2019.\r\n\r\nAfter learning to code in my second semester, I started using only Linux in 2016. I started with Ubuntu first, as usual. I then finished reading a book about \'Linux command Line\' (LINK:- http://linuxcommand.org/tlcl.php ) and did a course on Linux administration in Udemy (LINK:- <a href=\"https://www.udemy.com/linux-administration/learn/v4/\">https://www.udemy.com/linux-administration/learn/v4/</a> ).\r\n\r\nThen after tinkering with Ubuntu for months, I installed Arch Linux on my PC. I am now a happy user of Arch Linux for months now. So, I opened this blog to share some great tips and tutorials on Arch Linux.\r\n\r\nIn free time, I like to cycle to far away places.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;', 'About Me', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '24-revision-v1', '', '', '2017-10-20 14:52:12', '2017-10-20 09:22:12', '', 24, 'http://techwinky.com/24-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(32, 1, '2017-10-20 16:20:44', '2017-10-20 10:50:44', '<h1><img class=\"wp-image-26 alignright\" src=\"http://techwinky.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/10/IMG_20170219_110354-e1508489263874.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"183\" height=\"184\" />My Story:-</h1>\r\nHi! I am Sanjit Chakrabarti. I am doing Btech in computer engineering, graduating in 2019.\r\n\r\nAfter learning to code in my second semester, I started using only Linux in 2016. I started with Ubuntu first, as usual. I then finished reading a book about \'Linux command Line\' (LINK:- http://linuxcommand.org/tlcl.php ) and did a course on Linux administration in Udemy (LINK:- <a href=\"https://www.udemy.com/linux-administration/learn/v4/\">https://www.udemy.com/linux-administration/learn/v4/</a> ).\r\n\r\nThen after tinkering with Ubuntu for months, I installed Arch Linux on my PC to get more control over my OS. I am now a happy user of Arch Linux. So, I opened this blog to share some great tips and tutorials on Arch Linux.\r\n\r\nIn free time, I like to cycle far away places.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\nFollow me on:-\r\n\r\nTwitter - https://twitter.com/sujitsanjit?lang=en\r\n\r\nLinkedin - https://www.linkedin.com/in/sanjit-chakraborty-443152120/', 'About Me', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '24-revision-v1', '', '', '2017-10-20 16:20:44', '2017-10-20 10:50:44', '', 24, 'http://techwinky.com/24-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(33, 1, '2017-10-20 16:26:53', '2017-10-20 10:56:53', '<h1><img class=\"wp-image-26 alignright\" src=\"http://techwinky.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/10/IMG_20170219_110354-e1508489263874.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"183\" height=\"184\" />My Story:-</h1>\r\nHi! I am Sanjit Chakrabarti. I am doing Btech in computer engineering, graduating in 2019.\r\n\r\nAfter learning to code in my second semester, I started using only Linux in 2016. I started with Ubuntu first, as usual. I then finished reading this Book \'<a href=\"http://linuxcommand.org/tlcl.php\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Linux Command Line</a>\' and did a course on Linux administration in Udemy (LINK:- <a href=\"https://www.udemy.com/linux-administration/learn/v4/\">https://www.udemy.com/linux-administration/learn/v4/</a> ).\r\n\r\nThen after tinkering with Ubuntu for months, I installed Arch Linux on my PC to get more control over my OS. I am now a happy user of Arch Linux. So, I opened this blog to share some great tips and tutorials on Arch Linux.\r\n\r\nIn free time, I like to cycle far away places.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\nFollow me on:-\r\n\r\nTwitter - <a href=\"https://twitter.com/sujitsanjit?lang=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">@sujitsanjit</a>\r\n\r\nLinkedin - <a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/sanjit-chakraborty-443152120/\">sanjit-chakrabarti</a>', 'About Me', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '24-revision-v1', '', '', '2017-10-20 16:26:53', '2017-10-20 10:56:53', '', 24, 'http://techwinky.com/24-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
