(37, 1, '2017-10-20 16:34:05', '2017-10-20 11:04:05', '<h1><img class=\"wp-image-26 alignright\" src=\"http://techwinky.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/10/IMG_20170219_110354-e1508489263874.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"183\" height=\"184\" />My Story:-</h1>\r\nHi! I am Sanjit Chakrabarti. I am doing Btech in computer engineering, graduating in 2019.\r\n\r\nAfter learning to code in my second semester, I started using only Linux in 2016. I started with Ubuntu first, as usual. I then finished reading this Book \'<a href=\"http://linuxcommand.org/tlcl.php\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Linux Command Line</a>\' and did a course on Linux administration in Udemy (LINK:- <a href=\"https://www.udemy.com/linux-administration/learn/v4/\">https://www.udemy.com/linux-administration/learn/v4/</a> ).\r\n\r\nThen after tinkering with Ubuntu for months, I installed Arch Linux on my PC to get more control over my OS. I am now a happy user of Arch Linux. So, I opened this blog to share some great tips and tutorials on Arch Linux.\r\n\r\nIn free time, I like to cycle far away places.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\nFollow me on:-\r\n\r\nTwitter - <a href=\"https://twitter.com/sujitsanjit?lang=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">@sujitsanjit</a>\r\n\r\nLinkedin - <a href=\"http://www.linkedin.com/in/sanjit-chakraborty-443152120/\">http://www.linkedin.com/in/sanjit-chakraborty-443152120/</a>', 'About Me', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '24-revision-v1', '', '', '2017-10-20 16:34:05', '2017-10-20 11:04:05', '', 24, 'http://techwinky.com/24-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(41, 1, '2017-10-22 21:45:55', '2017-10-22 16:15:55', '<h2><img class=\"alignnone wp-image-65 size-full\" src=\"http://techwinky.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/10/download.png\" alt=\"Arch Linux Logo\" width=\"390\" height=\"129\" /></h2>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>1) <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Complete control</strong></span></h2>\r\n<h5>With Arch Linux, you get complete control over your OS. You will get to choose what program to install from <strong>A-Z</strong>. Nothing is <strong>Pre-installed</strong>. It\'s like building your own <strong>house</strong> where you will be your own architect. This is so cool as you get a sense of satisfaction after setting up your own OS.</h5>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>2) <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Way better customization</strong></span></h2>\r\n<h5>In Arch Linux, you even get to choose your <strong>Desktop environment</strong>. You can customize your computer, however, you want to. Make your PC even look like an <strong>APPLE MAC</strong>. You can change anything. You can even change the <strong>kernel</strong> (which is the heart of an OS) to run old software packages.</h5>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>3) <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>More in-depth knowledge about your PC</strong></span></h2>\r\n<h5>When you install Arch Linux, you have to install everything from the beginning, even the <strong>kernel</strong>. So, you get more in-depth knowledge about the<strong> working of an OS</strong>. You get a sense of an accomplishment as you start to understand <strong>low-level</strong> things off your PC.</h5>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>4) <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Rolling release</strong></span></h2>\r\n<h5>Arch Linux has this unique feature of \'<strong>Rolling Release</strong>\'. This means that your system will always get <strong>updated</strong> to the latest version without reinstalling the system. You will also get latest Linux Kernel before any other Linux Distribution (like UBUNTU).</h5>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>5) <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Maybe the biggest software repository</strong></span></h2>\r\n<h5>Arch Linux may be having the biggest software repository. I have yet to encounter any software packages which are not available on it (except Distro-specific software). This is due to its <strong>large community</strong> of open users, who are continuously working together to bring support to Arch Linux. Its <a href=\"https://aur.archlinux.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">AUR</a> repository set it apart from other Linux Distribution, where users can upload their own software package before it can be voted for transferring to the <a href=\"https://www.archlinux.org/packages/\">official repository</a>.</h5>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>6) <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><a href=\"https://wiki.archlinux.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Arch Wiki</a></span></h2>\r\n<h5>It\'s a great site for knowing anything about Arch Linux. <strong>Arch Wiki</strong> contains brief information about many software packages which can run in it, with their alternatives.</h5>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Conclusion</strong></span>:-</h2>\r\n<h5>In conclusion, switch to Arch Linux now if you want to get more <strong>control</strong> and more <strong>customization</strong> from your OS. You will get more <strong>in-depth knowledge</strong> about the working of your PC, with a great community of users and a <strong>large software repository</strong>. And also, not to mention, <strong>Arch Wiki</strong> to get more info on getting stuff work in Arch Linux with <strong>Rolling Release</strong> feature.</h5>', 'Top 6 reasons that why I use Arch Linux and you should too', '', 'publish', 'open', 'open', '', '6-reasons-arch-linux', '', '', '2018-02-11 23:42:04', '2018-02-11 18:12:04', '', 0, 'http://techwinky.com/?p=41', 0, 'post', '', 0),
(42, 1, '2017-10-21 12:52:03', '2017-10-21 07:22:03', '<h2>1) Complete control</h2>\r\nWith Arch Linux, you get complete control over your OS. You will get to choose the program that you would like to install.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;', '', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '41-revision-v1', '', '', '2017-10-21 12:52:03', '2017-10-21 07:22:03', '', 41, 'http://techwinky.com/41-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(46, 1, '2017-10-22 21:42:16', '2017-10-22 16:12:16', '<h2>1) Complete control</h2>\r\nWith Arch Linux, you get complete control over your OS. You will get to choose what program to install from <strong>A-Z</strong>. Nothing is <strong>Pre-installed</strong>. It\'s like building your own <strong>house</strong> where you will be your own architect.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>2) Way better customization</h2>\r\nIn Arch Linux, you even get to choose your <strong>Desktop environment</strong>. You can customize your computer, however you want to. Make your PC even look like an <strong>APPLE MAC</strong>. You can change anything. You can even change the <strong>kernel</strong> (which is the heart of an OS) to run old software packages.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2><strong>3) More in-depth knowledge about your PC</strong></h2>\r\nWhen you install Arch Linux, you have to install everything from the beginning, even the <strong>kernel</strong>. So, you get more in-depth knowledge about the<strong> working of an OS</strong>. You get a sense of an accomplishment as you start to understand <strong>low-level</strong> things of your PC.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>4) Rolling release</h2>\r\nArch Linux has this unique feature of \'<strong>Rolling Release</strong>\'. This means that your system will always get <strong>updated</strong> to the latest version without reinstalling the system. You will also get latest Linux Kernel before any other Linux Distribution (like UBUNTU).\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>5) Maybe the biggest software repository</h2>\r\nArch Linux may be having the biggest software repository. I have yet to encounter any software packages which is not available in Arch Linux (except Distro-specific software). This is due to its <strong>large community</strong> of open users, who are continuously work together to bring support to Arch Linux.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>6) <a href=\"https://wiki.archlinux.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Arch Wiki</a></h2>\r\nIt\'s a great site for knowing anything about Arch Linux. <strong>Arch Wiki</strong> contains brief information about many software packages which can run in Arch Linux, with their alternatives.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>Conclusion:-</h2>\r\nIn conclusion, switch to Arch Linux now if you want to get more <strong>control</strong> and more <strong>customization</strong> from your OS. You will get more<strong> in-depth knowledge</strong> about the working of your PC, with a <strong>great community</strong> of users and a large software repository. And also, not to mention, <strong>Arch Wiki</strong> to get more info on getting stuff work in Arch Linux with <strong>Rolling Release</strong> feature.', 'Top 6 reasons for switching to Arch Linux', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '41-revision-v1', '', '', '2017-10-22 21:42:16', '2017-10-22 16:12:16', '', 41, 'http://techwinky.com/41-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
