for knowing anything about Arch Linux. <strong>Arch Wiki</strong> contains brief information about many software packages which can run in Arch Linux, with their alternatives.</h3>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>Conclusion:-</h2>\r\n<h3><strong>In conclusion, switch to Arch Linux now if you want to get more </strong>control<strong> and more customization from your OS. You will get more in-depth knowledge about the working of your PC, with a great community of users and a large software repository. And also, not to mention, Arch Wiki to get more info on getting stuff work in Arch Linux with Rolling Release feature.</strong></h3>', 'Top 6 reasons for switching to Arch Linux', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '41-revision-v1', '', '', '2017-10-22 21:50:08', '2017-10-22 16:20:08', '', 41, 'http://techwinky.com/41-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(53, 1, '2017-10-22 21:51:10', '2017-10-22 16:21:10', '<h2>1) <strong>Complete control</strong></h2>\r\n<h3>With Arch Linux, you get complete control over your OS. You will get to choose what program to install from <strong>A-Z</strong>. Nothing is <strong>Pre-installed</strong>. It\'s like building your own <strong>house</strong> where you will be your own architect.</h3>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>2) <strong>Way better customization</strong></h2>\r\n<h3>In Arch Linux, you even get to choose your <strong>Desktop environment</strong>. You can customize your computer, however, you want to. Make your PC even look like an <strong>APPLE MAC</strong>. You can change anything. You can even change the <strong>kernel</strong> (which is the heart of an OS) to run old software packages.</h3>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>3) <strong>More in-depth knowledge about your PC</strong></h2>\r\n<h3>When you install Arch Linux, you have to install everything from the beginning, even the <strong>kernel</strong>. So, you get more in-depth knowledge about the<strong> working of an OS</strong>. You get a sense of an accomplishment as you start to understand <strong>low-level</strong> things off your PC.</h3>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>4)<strong> Rolling release</strong></h2>\r\n<h3>Arch Linux has this unique feature of \'<strong>Rolling Release</strong>\'. This means that your system will always get <strong>updated</strong> to the latest version without reinstalling the system. You will also get latest Linux Kernel before any other Linux Distribution (like UBUNTU).</h3>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>5) <strong>Maybe the biggest software repository</strong></h2>\r\n<h3>Arch Linux may be having the biggest software repository. I have yet to encounter any software packages which are not available on Arch Linux (except Distro-specific software). This is due to its <strong>large community</strong> of open users, who are continuously working together to bring support to Arch Linux.</h3>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>6) <a href=\"https://wiki.archlinux.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Arch Wiki</a></h2>\r\n<h3>It\'s a great site for knowing anything about Arch Linux. <strong>Arch Wiki</strong> contains brief information about many software packages which can run in Arch Linux, with their alternatives.</h3>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2><strong>Conclusion</strong>:-</h2>\r\n<h3><strong>In conclusion, switch to Arch Linux now if you want to get more </strong>control<strong> and more customization from your OS. You will get more in-depth knowledge about the working of your PC, with a great community of users and a large software repository. And also, not to mention, Arch Wiki to get more info on getting stuff work in Arch Linux with Rolling Release feature.</strong></h3>', 'Top 6 reasons for switching to Arch Linux', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '41-revision-v1', '', '', '2017-10-22 21:51:10', '2017-10-22 16:21:10', '', 41, 'http://techwinky.com/41-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
