available on Arch Linux (except Distro-specific software). This is due to its <strong>large community</strong> of open users, who are continuously working together to bring support to Arch Linux.</h3>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>6) <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><a href=\"https://wiki.archlinux.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Arch Wiki</a></span></h2>\r\n<h3>It\'s a great site for knowing anything about Arch Linux. <strong>Arch Wiki</strong> contains brief information about many software packages which can run in Arch Linux, with their alternatives.</h3>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Conclusion</strong></span>:-</h2>\r\n<h3><strong>In conclusion, switch to Arch Linux now if you want to get more </strong>control<strong> and more customization from your OS. You will get more in-depth knowledge about the working of your PC, with a great community of users and a large software repository. And also, not to mention, Arch Wiki to get more info on getting stuff work in Arch Linux with Rolling Release feature.</strong></h3>', 'Top 6 reasons for switching to Arch Linux', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '41-revision-v1', '', '', '2017-10-22 21:52:13', '2017-10-22 16:22:13', '', 41, 'http://techwinky.com/41-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
