ository. I have yet to encounter any software packages which are not available on Arch Linux (except Distro-specific software). This is due to its <strong>large community</strong> of open users, who are continuously working together to bring support to Arch Linux.</h5>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>6) <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><a href=\"https://wiki.archlinux.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Arch Wiki</a></span></h2>\r\n<h5>It\'s a great site for knowing anything about Arch Linux. <strong>Arch Wiki</strong> contains brief information about many software packages which can run in Arch Linux, with their alternatives.</h5>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Conclusion</strong></span>:-</h2>\r\n<h5><strong>In conclusion, switch to Arch Linux now if you want to get more </strong>control<strong> and more customization from your OS. You will get more in-depth knowledge about the working of your PC, with a great community of users and a large software repository. And also, not to mention, Arch Wiki to get more info on getting stuff work in Arch Linux with Rolling Release feature.</strong></h5>', 'Top 6 reasons for switching to Arch Linux', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '41-revision-v1', '', '', '2017-10-22 21:54:18', '2017-10-22 16:24:18', '', 41, 'http://techwinky.com/41-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(59, 1, '2017-10-22 21:58:34', '2017-10-22 16:28:34', '<h1><img class=\"wp-image-26 alignright\" src=\"http://techwinky.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/10/IMG_20170219_110354-e1508489263874.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"183\" height=\"184\" />My Story:-</h1>\r\n<h5>Hi! I am Sanjit Chakrabarti. I am doing Btech in computer engineering, graduating in 2019.</h5>\r\n<h5>After learning to code in my second semester, I started using only Linux in 2016. I started with Ubuntu first, as usual. I then finished reading this Book \'<a href=\"http://linuxcommand.org/tlcl.php\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Linux Command Line</a>\' and did a course on Linux administration in Udemy (LINK:- <a href=\"https://www.udemy.com/linux-administration/learn/v4/\">https://www.udemy.com/linux-administration/learn/v4/</a> ).</h5>\r\n<h5>Then after tinkering with Ubuntu for months, I installed Arch Linux on my PC to get more control over my OS. I am now a happy user of Arch Linux. So, I opened this blog to share some great tips and tutorials on Arch Linux. Hope to make Arch Linux as simple as possible.</h5>\r\n<h5>In free time, I like to cycle far away places.</h5>\r\n<h5></h5>\r\n<h5>Follow me on:-</h5>\r\n<h5>Twitter - <a href=\"https://twitter.com/sujitsanjit?lang=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">@sujitsanjit</a></h5>\r\n<h5>Linkedin - <a href=\"http://www.linkedin.com/in/sanjit-chakraborty-443152120/\">http://www.linkedin.com/in/sanjit-chakraborty-443152120/</a></h5>', 'About Me', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '24-revision-v1', '', '', '2017-10-22 21:58:34', '2017-10-22 16:28:34', '', 24, 'http://techwinky.com/24-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(60, 1, '2017-10-22 22:06:17', '2017-10-22 16:36:17', '<h1><img class=\"wp-image-26 alignright\" src=\"http://techwinky.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/10/IMG_20170219_110354-e1508489263874.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"183\" height=\"184\" />My Story:-</h1>\r\n<h5>Hi! I am Sanjit Chakrabarti. I am doing Btech in computer engineering, graduating in 2019.</h5>\r\n<h5>After learning to code in my second semester, I started using only Linux in 2016. I started with Ubuntu first, as usual. I then finished reading this Book \'<a href=\"http://linuxcommand.org/tlcl.php\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Linux Command Line</a>\' and did a course on Linux administration in Udemy (LINK:- <a href=\"https://www.udemy.com/linux-administration/learn/v4/\">https://www.udemy.com/linux-administration/learn/v4/</a> ).</h5>\r\n<h5>Then after tinkering with Ubuntu for months, I installed Arch Linux on my PC to get more control over my OS. I am now a happy user of Arch Linux. So, I opened this blog to share some great tips and tutorials on Arch Linux. Hope to make Arch Linux as simple as possible.</h5>\r\n<h5>In free time, I like to cycle far away places.</h5>\r\n<h5></h5>\r\n<h5>Follow me on:-</h5>\r\n<h5>Twitter - <a href=\"https://twitter.com/sujitsanjit?lang=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">@sujitsanjit</a></h5>\r\n<h5>Linkedin - http://www.linkedin.com/in/sanjit-chakrabarti-pro</h5>', 'About Me', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '24-revision-v1', '', '', '2017-10-22 22:06:17', '2017-10-22 16:36:17', '', 24, 'http://techwinky.com/24-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(61, 1, '2017-10-22 22:07:00', '2017-10-22 16:37:00', '<h1><img class=\"wp-image-26 alignright\" src=\"http://techwinky.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/10/IMG_20170219_110354-e1508489263874.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"183\" height=\"184\" />My Story:-</h1>\r\n<h5>Hi! I am Sanjit Chakrabarti. I am doing Btech in computer engineering, graduating in 2019.</h5>\r\n<h5>After learning to code in my second semester, I started using only Linux in 2016. I started with Ubuntu first, as usual. I then finished reading this Book \'<a href=\"http://linuxcommand.org/tlcl.php\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Linux Command Line</a>\' and did a course on Linux administration in Udemy (LINK:- <a href=\"https://www.udemy.com/linux-administration/learn/v4/\">https://www.udemy.com/linux-administration/learn/v4/</a> ).</h5>\r\n<h5>Then after tinkering with Ubuntu for months, I installed Arch Linux on my PC to get more control over my OS. I am now a happy user of Arch Linux. So, I opened this blog to share some great tips and tutorials on Arch Linux. Hope to make Arch Linux as simple as possible.</h5>\r\n<h5>In free time, I like to cycle far away places.</h5>\r\n<h5></h5>\r\n<h5>Follow me on:-</h5>\r\n<h5>Twitter - <a href=\"https://twitter.com/sujitsanjit?lang=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">@sujitsanjit</a></h5>\r\n<h5>Linkedin - <a href=\"http://www.linkedin.com/in/sanjit-chakrabarti-pro\">sanjit-chakrabarti-pro</a></h5>', 'About Me', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '24-revision-v1', '', '', '2017-10-22 22:07:00', '2017-10-22 16:37:00', '', 24, 'http://techwinky.com/24-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(62, 1, '2017-10-22 22:08:45', '2017-10-22 16:38:45', '<h2></h2>\r\n<h2>1) <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Complete control</strong></span></h2>\r\n<h5>With Arch Linux, you get complete control over your OS. You will get to choose what program to install from <strong>A-Z</strong>. Nothing is <strong>Pre-installed</strong>. It\'s like building your own <strong>house</strong> where you will be your own architect.</h5>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>2) <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Way better customization</strong></span></h2>\r\n<h5>In Arch Linux, you even get to choose your <strong>Desktop environment</strong>. You can customize your computer, however, you want to. Make your PC even look like an <strong>APPLE MAC</strong>. You can change anything. You can even change the <strong>kernel</strong> (which is the heart of an OS) to run old software packages.</h5>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>3) <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>More in-depth knowledge about your PC</strong></span></h2>\r\n<h5>When you install Arch Linux, you have to install everything from the beginning, even the <strong>kernel</strong>. So, you get more in-depth knowledge about the<strong> working of an OS</strong>. You get a sense of an accomplishment as you start to understand <strong>low-level</strong> things off your PC.</h5>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>4) <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Rolling release</strong></span></h2>\r\n<h5>Arch Linux has this unique feature of \'<strong>Rolling Release</strong>\'. This means that your system will always get <strong>updated</strong> to the latest version without reinstalling the system. You will also get latest Linux Kernel before any other Linux Distribution (like UBUNTU).</h5>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>5) <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Maybe the biggest software repository</strong></span></h2>\r\n<h5>Arch Linux may be having the biggest software repository. I have yet to encounter any software packages which are not available on Arch Linux (except Distro-specific software). This is due to its <strong>large community</strong> of open users, who are continuously working together to bring support to Arch Linux.</h5>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>6) <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><a href=\"https://wiki.archlinux.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Arch Wiki</a></span></h2>\r\n<h5>It\'s a great site for knowing anything about Arch Linux. <strong>Arch Wiki</strong> contains brief information about many software packages which can run in Arch Linux, with their alternatives.</h5>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Conclusion</strong></span>:-</h2>\r\n<h5>In conclusion, switch to Arch Linux now if you want to get more <strong>control</strong> and more <strong>customization</strong> from your OS. You will get more <strong>in-depth knowledge</strong> about the working of your PC, with a great community of users and a <strong>large software repository</strong>. And also, not to mention, <strong>Arch Wiki</strong> to get more info on getting stuff work in Arch Linux with <strong>Rolling Release</strong> feature.</h5>', 'Top 6 reasons for switching to Arch Linux', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '41-revision-v1', '', '', '2017-10-22 22:08:45', '2017-10-22 16:38:45', '', 41, 'http://techwinky.com/41-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(64, 1, '2017-10-22 22:23:36', '2017-10-22 16:53:36', '<h2></h2>\r\n<h2>1) <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Complete control</strong></span></h2>\r\n<h5>With Arch Linux, you get complete control over your OS. You will get to choose what program to install from <strong>A-Z</strong>. Nothing is <strong>Pre-installed</strong>. It\'s like building your own <strong>house</strong> where you will be your own architect.</h5>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>2) <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Way better customization</strong></span></h2>\r\n<h5>In Arch Linux, you even get to choose your <strong>Desktop environment</strong>. You can customize your computer, however, you want to. Make your PC even look like an <strong>APPLE MAC</strong>. You can change anything. You can even change the <strong>kernel</strong> (which is the heart of an OS) to run old software packages.</h5>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>3) <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>More in-depth knowledge about your PC</strong></span></h2>\r\n<h5>When you install Arch Linux, you have to install everything from the beginning, even the <strong>kernel</strong>. So, you get more in-depth knowledge about the<strong> working of an OS</strong>. You get a sense of an accomplishment as you start to understand <strong>low-level</strong> things off your PC.</h5>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>4) <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Rolling release</strong></span></h2>\r\n<h5>Arch Linux has this unique feature of \'<strong>Rolling Release</strong>\'. This means that your system will always get <strong>updated</strong> to the latest version without reinstalling the system. You will also get latest Linux Kernel before any other Linux Distribution (like UBUNTU).</h5>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>5) <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Maybe the biggest software repository</strong></span></h2>\r\n<h5>Arch Linux may be having the biggest software repository. I have yet to encounter any software packages which are not available on Arch Linux (except Distro-specific software). This is due to its <strong>large community</strong> of open users, who are continuously working together to bring support to Arch Linux. Its <a href=\"https://aur.archlinux.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">AUR</a> repository set it apart from other Linux Distribution, where users can upload their own software package before it can be voted for transferring to the <a href=\"https://www.archlinux.org/packages/\">official repository</a>.</h5>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>6) <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><a href=\"https://wiki.archlinux.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Arch Wiki</a></span></h2>\r\n<h5>It\'s a great site for knowing anything about Arch Linux. <strong>Arch Wiki</strong> contains brief information about many software packages which can run in Arch Linux, with their alternatives.</h5>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Conclusion</strong></span>:-</h2>\r\n<h5>In conclusion, switch to Arch Linux now if you want to get more <strong>control</strong> and more <strong>customization</strong> from your OS. You will get more <strong>in-depth knowledge</strong> about the working of your PC, with a great community of users and a <strong>large software repository</strong>. And also, not to mention, <strong>Arch Wiki</strong> to get more info on getting stuff work in Arch Linux with <strong>Rolling Release</strong> feature.</h5>', 'Top 6 reasons that why I use Arch Linux and you should too', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '41-revision-v1', '', '', '2017-10-22 22:23:36', '2017-10-22 16:53:36', '', 41, 'http://techwinky.com/41-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(65, 1, '2017-10-22 22:25:29', '2017-10-22 16:55:29', '', 'download', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'closed', '', 'download', '', '', '2017-10-22 22:25:29', '2017-10-22 16:55:29', '', 41, 'http://techwinky.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/10/download.png', 0, 'attachment', 'image/png', 0),
(66, 1, '2017-10-22 22:29:21', '2017-10-22 16:59:21', '<h2><img class=\"alignnone wp-image-65 size-full\" src=\"http://techwinky.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/10/download.png\" alt=\"Arch Linux Logo\" width=\"390\" height=\"129\" /></h2>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>1) <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Complete control</strong></span></h2>\r\n<h5>With Arch Linux, you get complete control over your OS. You will get to choose what program to install from <strong>A-Z</strong>. Nothing is <strong>Pre-installed</strong>. It\'s like building your own <strong>house</strong> where you will be your own architect.</h5>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>2) <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Way better customization</strong></span></h2>\r\n<h5>In Arch Linux, you even get to choose your <strong>Desktop environment</strong>. You can customize your computer, however, you want to. Make your PC even look like an <strong>APPLE MAC</strong>. You can change anything. You can even change the <strong>kernel</strong> (which is the heart of an OS) to run old software packages.</h5>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>3) <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>More in-depth knowledge about your PC</strong></span></h2>\r\n<h5>When you install Arch Linux, you have to install everything from the beginning, even the <strong>kernel</strong>. So, you get more in-depth knowledge about the<strong> working of an OS</strong>. You get a sense of an accomplishment as you start to understand <strong>low-level</strong> things off your PC.</h5>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>4) <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Rolling release</strong></span></h2>\r\n<h5>Arch Linux has this unique feature of \'<strong>Rolling Release</strong>\'. This means that your system will always get <strong>updated</strong> to the latest version without reinstalling the system. You will also get latest Linux Kernel before any other Linux Distribution (like UBUNTU).</h5>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>5) <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Maybe the biggest software repository</strong></span></h2>\r\n<h5>Arch Linux may be having the biggest software repository. I have yet to encounter any software packages which are not available on it (except Distro-specific software). This is due to its <strong>large community</strong> of open users, who are continuously working together to bring support to Arch Linux. Its <a href=\"https://aur.archlinux.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">AUR</a> repository set it apart from other Linux Distribution, where users can upload their own software package before it can be voted for transferring to the <a href=\"https://www.archlinux.org/packages/\">official repository</a>.</h5>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>6) <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><a href=\"https://wiki.archlinux.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Arch Wiki</a></span></h2>\r\n<h5>It\'s a great site for knowing anything about Arch Linux. <strong>Arch Wiki</strong> contains brief information about many software packages which can run in it, with their alternatives.</h5>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Conclusion</strong></span>:-</h2>\r\n<h5>In conclusion, switch to Arch Linux now if you want to get more <strong>control</strong> and more <strong>customization</strong> from your OS. You will get more <strong>in-depth knowledge</strong> about the working of your PC, with a great community of users and a <strong>large software repository</strong>. And also, not to mention, <strong>Arch Wiki</strong> to get more info on getting stuff work in Arch Linux with <strong>Rolling Release</strong> feature.</h5>', 'Top 6 reasons that why I use Arch Linux and you should too', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '41-revision-v1', '', '', '2017-10-22 22:29:21', '2017-10-22 16:59:21', '', 41, 'http://techwinky.com/41-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(67, 1, '2017-10-22 22:32:53', '2017-10-22 17:02:53', '<h2><img class=\"alignnone wp-image-65 size-full\" src=\"http://techwinky.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/10/download.png\" alt=\"Arch Linux Logo\" width=\"390\" height=\"129\" /></h2>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>1) <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Complete control</strong></span></h2>\r\n<h5>With Arch Linux, you get complete control over your OS. You will get to choose what program to install from <strong>A-Z</strong>. Nothing is <strong>Pre-installed</strong>. It\'s like building your own <strong>house</strong> where you will be your own architect. This is so cool as you get a sense of satisfaction after setting up your own OS.</h5>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>2) <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Way better customization</strong></span></h2>\r\n<h5>In Arch Linux, you even get to choose your <strong>Desktop environment</strong>. You can customize your computer, however, you want to. Make your PC even look like an <strong>APPLE MAC</strong>. You can change anything. You can even change the <strong>kernel</strong> (which is the heart of an OS) to run old software packages.</h5>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>3) <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>More in-depth knowledge about your PC</strong></span></h2>\r\n<h5>When you install Arch Linux, you have to install everything from the beginning, even the <strong>kernel</strong>. So, you get more in-depth knowledge about the<strong> working of an OS</strong>. You get a sense of an accomplishment as you start to understand <strong>low-level</strong> things off your PC.</h5>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>4) <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Rolling release</strong></span></h2>\r\n<h5>Arch Linux has this unique feature of \'<strong>Rolling Release</strong>\'. This means that your system will always get <strong>updated</strong> to the latest version without reinstalling the system. You will also get latest Linux Kernel before any other Linux Distribution (like UBUNTU).</h5>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>5) <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Maybe the biggest software repository</strong></span></h2>\r\n<h5>Arch Linux may be having the biggest software repository. I have yet to encounter any software packages which are not available on it (except Distro-specific software). This is due to its <strong>large community</strong> of open users, who are continuously working together to bring support to Arch Linux. Its <a href=\"https://aur.archlinux.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">AUR</a> repository set it apart from other Linux Distribution, where users can upload their own software package before it can be voted for transferring to the <a href=\"https://www.archlinux.org/packages/\">official repository</a>.</h5>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2>6) <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><a href=\"https://wiki.archlinux.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Arch Wiki</a></span></h2>\r\n<h5>It\'s a great site for knowing anything about Arch Linux. <strong>Arch Wiki</strong> contains brief information about many software packages which can run in it, with their alternatives.</h5>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Conclusion</strong></span>:-</h2>\r\n<h5>In conclusion, switch to Arch Linux now if you want to get more <strong>control</strong> and more <strong>customization</strong> from your OS. You will get more <strong>in-depth knowledge</strong> about the working of your PC, with a great community of users and a <strong>large software repository</strong>. And also, not to mention, <strong>Arch Wiki</strong> to get more info on getting stuff work in Arch Linux with <strong>Rolling Release</strong> feature.</h5>', 'Top 6 reasons that why I use Arch Linux and you should too', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '41-revision-v1', '', '', '2017-10-22 22:32:53', '2017-10-22 17:02:53', '', 41, 'http://techwinky.com/41-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(72, 2, '2018-01-19 01:23:56', '2018-01-18 19:53:56', '<h5>Are you a computer geek or an employee, who spend too much time using Google Chrome?</h5>\r\n<h5>Then, this article is for you. These important shortcuts will speed up of your productivity and hence, reduce anxiety and stress. Try them to see the results.</h5>\r\n<h5><u>Before using shortcuts you should be aware of these concepts:-</u></h5>\r\n<ol>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5> Difference between TAB &amp; WINDOW.</h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5> Chrome menu</h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5> Bookmark manager</h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5> Chrome task manager (For programmers and geeks)</h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5> Find bar</h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5> Developer tool (For programmers and geeks)</h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5> Chrome user account</h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5> Search bar/Address Bar</h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<h5></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">PART-1</span></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">OPERATIONS ON WINDOW AND TABS</span></h5>\r\n<h5>OPEN OPERATION:-</h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Open a new window- <strong>ctrl+n</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Open a new window in incognito mode- <strong>ctrl+shift+n</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Open a new tab-<strong> ctrl+t</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Reopen previously closed tab-<strong> ctrl+shift+t</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5>NAVIGATION OPERATION:-</h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Jump to next open tab-<strong>ctrl+tab</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Jump to previously open tab-<strong>ctrl+shift+tab</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Go to a specific tab- <strong>ctrl+\'tab number\'</strong> (Eg- ctrl+1 for the Ist tab.  Will work for 1-8 only)</h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Go to last tab- <strong>ctrl+9</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Go to the previous tab from current tab- <strong>alt+left arrow</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Go to the next tab from current tab-<strong> alt+right bar</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5>CLOSE OPERATION:-</h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Close the current tab-<strong>ctrl+w</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Close the current window-<strong>alt+f4</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Close browser with all opened tabs-<strong>ctrl+shift+w</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Quite Google chrome-<strong>ctrl+shift+q</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5>MINIMISE OPERATION:-</h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Minimize the current window-<strong>alt+space+n</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Maximise the already minimized window-<strong>alt+space+x</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"> <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Part-2</span></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">SMART SEARCH TECHNIQUE  (Playing around address bar)</span></h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Search with a specific search engine -<strong>\"search engine name\"+\"search term\"+tab+enter</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Search with Google only.- <strong>\"search term\"+alt+enter</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Add automatically www and .com in address bar- <strong>\"site name\"+ctrl+enter</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Go to address bar directly and search-<strong>ctrl+e</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Remove prediction from address bar- <strong>\"Down arrow to highlight\" +shift+delete</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"> <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Part-3</span></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">FOR DEVELOPERS</span></h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Chrome menu-<strong>alt+e or alt+f</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Chrome task manager-<strong>shift+esc</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Open the find bar to search the current page-<strong>ctrl+f</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Jump to next match while finding-<strong>ctrl+g</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Jump to the previous match while finding-<strong>ctrl+shift+g</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Open developer tools-<strong>ctrl+shift+i</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Display non-editable HTML page-<strong>ctrl+u</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Log in with different user-<strong>ctrl+shift+m</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5>For More advanced developer shortcuts:-</h5>\r\n<h5><a href=\"http://www.elves.in\">click here</a></h5>\r\n<h5></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"> <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Part-4</span></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">BOOKMARK</span>,<span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"> HISTORY &amp; DOWNLOADS</span></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: left;\">BOOKMARK OPERATION:-</h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Toggle (Show or hide) Bookmark bar-<strong>ctrl+shift+b</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Open Bookmark manager-<strong>ctrl+shift+o</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Save current page to your Bookmark-<strong>ctrl+b</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Save all opened tabs as a Bookmark in New folder-<strong>ctrl+shift+d</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: left;\">HISTORY OPERATION:-</h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Open the history page-<strong>ctrl+h</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Open \'clear all browsing data\' option-<strong>ctrl+shift+delete</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: left;\">DOWNLOAD OPERATION:-</h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Open download page-<strong>ctrl+j</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"> <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Part-5</span></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">ESSENTIALS</span></h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Print current page-<strong>ctrl+p</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Save the current page-<strong>ctrl+s</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Reload the page-<strong>ctrl+r</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Stop the page to load-<strong>esc</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Open a file in chrome-<strong>ctrl+o</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Toggle fullscreen-<strong>f11</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Scroll down-<strong>space</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Scroll up-<strong>shift+space</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Scroll horizontally-<strong>shift+scroll mouse wheel</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Part-6</span></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">OPERATION WITH MOUSE </span></h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">\r\n<h5>Zoom in-<strong>ctrl+wheel up</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">\r\n<h5>Zoom out-<strong>ctrl+wheel down</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">\r\n<h5>Download the target link-<strong>alt+click a link</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">\r\n<h5>Open a link in current tab-<strong>drag a link to tab</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">\r\n<h5>Open a link in New background tab-<strong>ctrl+click the link</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">\r\n<h5>Open a link in New window-<strong>shift+click the link</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5></h5>\r\n<h5></h5>', 'Useful CHROME keyboard shortcuts to speed up your productivity', '', 'publish', 'open', 'open', '', 'useful-chrome-keyboard-shortcuts-to-speed-up-your-productivity', '', '', '2018-02-12 00:04:09', '2018-02-11 18:34:09', '', 0, 'http://techwinky.com/?p=72', 0, 'post', '', 0),
(73, 1, '2018-01-19 01:23:56', '2018-01-18 19:53:56', 'Are you a computer geek or a employee that so spend too much time in chrome. So this article is for you. This important shortcuts will speed up of your work hence reduce anxiety and frustration.Use it and see the result.\n\n<u>Before using this shortcuts you should aware about these</u>\n\n1. Difference between TAB &amp; WINDOW.\n\n2. Chrome menu\n\n3. Bookmark manger\n\n4. Chrome task manager (For programmers and geeks)\n\n5. Find bar\n\n6. Developer tool (For programmers and geeks)\n\n7. Chrome user account\n\n8.Search bar/Address Bar                       \n<h3><b>Part-1</b></h3>\n<h3><b>Operation on chrome Window</b></h3>\n<h4>OPENING</h4>\nOpen a new window.     <b>ctrl+n</b>\n\nOpen a new window in incognito mode.  <b>ctrl+shift+n</b>\n\nOpen a new tab.  <b>Ctrl+t</b>\n\nReopen previous closed tab    <b>ctrl+shift+t</b>\n<h4>NAVIGATING THROUGH TABS</h4>\nJump to next open tab   <b>ctrl+tab</b>\n\nJump to previous open tab <b>ctrl+shift+tab</b>\n\nGo to specify tab <b>ctrl+tab no(  </b>like<b> </b>ctrl<b>+</b>1 for first tab,it will work for 1-8 only<b>)</b>\n\nGo to last tab <b>ctrl+9</b>\n\nGo back in same tab <b>alt+left arrow </b>\n\nGo forward in same tab <b>alt+right bar</b>\n<h4>CLOSINGS</h4>\nClose the current tab (Tab in which in you are working) <b>ctrl+w</b>\n\nClose the current window <b>alt+f4</b>\n\nClose browser and all open tabs <b>ctrl+shift+w</b>\n\nQuite Google chrome <b>ctrl+shift+q</b>\n<h4>MINIMISE</h4>\nMinimize the current window <b>alt+space+n</b>\n\nMaximise the already minimised window <b>alt+space+x</b>\n<h2>Part-2</h2>\n<h3><b>Smart search technique (Playing around addr</b>ess bar)</h3>\nSearch with a specific search engine \"search<b> engine name\"+\"search term\"+tab+enter</b>\n\nSearch with Google only. <b>\"search term\"+alt+ent</b>er\n\nAdd automatically <b>www</b> and <b>.com</b> and search store \"<b>site name\"+ctrl+enter</b>\n\nGo to search box directly and search <b>ctrl+e</b>\n\nRemove prediction from address bar. <b>\"Down arrow to highlight\" +shift+delete</b>\n<h2>Part-3</h2>\n<h3>For developers</h3>\nChrome menu.  <b>alt+e  \"or\" alt+f</b>\n\nChrome task manager <b>shift+esc</b>\n\nOpen the find bar to search the current page <b>ctrl+f</b>\n\nJump to next match in find search box <b>Ctrl+g</b>\n\nJump to previous match in find search box <b>Ctrl+shift+g</b>\n\nOpen developer tool <b>ctrl+shift+i</b>\n\nDisplay non editable HTML page <b>ctrl+u</b>\n\nLog in different user <b>ctrl+shift+m</b>\n<h4>For More advanced developer short cut <a href=\"elves.in\">click here</a></h4>\n<h2>Part-4</h2>\n<h3>Bookmarks,download &amp; history</h3>\n<h4>Bookmark</h4>\nToggle (Show or hide) Bookmark bar <b>ctrl+shift+b</b>\n\nOpen Bookmark manger <b>ctrl+shift+o</b>\n\nSave current page to your Bookmark <b>c</b><b><b>trl+b</b></b>\n\n<b>Save all open tabs</b> as a Bookmark in New folder <b>ctrl+shift+d</b>\n\n\n<h4>History</h4>\nOpen the history page <b>ctrl+h</b>\n\nOpen clear all browsing data option <b>Ctrl+shift+delete</b>\n<h4>Download</h4>\nOpen download page <b>ctrl+j</b>\n<h2>Part-5</h2>\nEssentials\n\nPrint current page <b>ctrl+p</b>\n\nSave the current page <b>ctrl+s</b>\n\nReload the page <b>ctrl+r</b>\n\nStop the page to load <b>esc</b>\n\nOpen a file in chrome <b>ctrl+o</b>\n\nToggle fullscreen <b>f11</b>\n\nScroll down <b>space</b>\n\nScroll up <b>shift+space</b>\n\nScroll horizontally <b>shift+scroll mouse wheel</b>\n<h2>Part-4</h2>\n<b>WITH MOUSE </b>\n\n\nzoom in <b>ctrl+wheel up </b>\nZoom out <b>ctrl+wheel down</b>\n\nDownload the target of link <b>alt+click a link</b>\n\nOpen a link in current tab <b>drag a link to tab</b>\n\nOpen a link in New background tab <b>ctrl+click the link</b>\n\nOpen a link in New window <b>shift+click the link</b>', 'Usefull CHROME keyboard Shortcuts to speed up your productivity', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '72-revision-v1', '', '', '2018-01-19 01:23:56', '2018-01-18 19:53:56', '', 72, 'http://techwinky.com/72-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(75, 1, '2018-02-12 00:03:55', '2018-02-11 18:33:55', '<h5>Are you a computer geek or an employee, who spend too much time using Google Chrome?</h5>\r\n<h5>Then, this article is for you. These important shortcuts will speed up of your productivity and hence, reduce anxiety and stress. Try them to see the results.</h5>\r\n<h5><u>Before using shortcuts you should be aware of these concepts:-</u></h5>\r\n<ol>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5> Difference between TAB &amp; WINDOW.</h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5> Chrome menu</h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5> Bookmark manager</h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5> Chrome task manager (For programmers and geeks)</h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5> Find bar</h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5> Developer tool (For programmers and geeks)</h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5> Chrome user account</h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5> Search bar/Address Bar</h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<h5></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">PART-1</span></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">OPERATIONS ON WINDOW AND TABS</span></h5>\r\n<h5>OPEN OPERATION:-</h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Open a new window- <strong>ctrl+n</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Open a new window in incognito mode- <strong>ctrl+shift+n</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Open a new tab-<strong> ctrl+t</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Reopen previously closed tab-<strong> ctrl+shift+t</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5>NAVIGATION OPERATION:-</h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Jump to next open tab-<strong>ctrl+tab</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Jump to previously open tab-<strong>ctrl+shift+tab</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Go to a specific tab- <strong>ctrl+\'tab number\'</strong> (Eg- ctrl+1 for the Ist tab.  Will work for 1-8 only)</h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Go to last tab- <strong>ctrl+9</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Go to the previous tab from current tab- <strong>alt+left arrow</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Go to the next tab from current tab-<strong> alt+right bar</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5>CLOSE OPERATION:-</h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Close the current tab-<strong>ctrl+w</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Close the current window-<strong>alt+f4</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Close browser with all opened tabs-<strong>ctrl+shift+w</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Quite Google chrome-<strong>ctrl+shift+q</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5>MINIMISE OPERATION:-</h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Minimize the current window-<strong>alt+space+n</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Maximise the already minimized window-<strong>alt+space+x</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"> <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Part-2</span></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">SMART SEARCH TECHNIQUE  (Playing around address bar)</span></h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Search with a specific search engine -<strong>\"search engine name\"+\"search term\"+tab+enter</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Search with Google only.- <strong>\"search term\"+alt+enter</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Add automatically www and .com in address bar- <strong>\"site name\"+ctrl+enter</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Go to address bar directly and search-<strong>ctrl+e</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Remove prediction from address bar- <strong>\"Down arrow to highlight\" +shift+delete</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"> <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Part-3</span></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">FOR DEVELOPERS</span></h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Chrome menu-<strong>alt+e or alt+f</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Chrome task manager-<strong>shift+esc</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Open the find bar to search the current page-<strong>ctrl+f</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Jump to next match while finding-<strong>ctrl+g</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Jump to the previous match while finding-<strong>ctrl+shift+g</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Open developer tools-<strong>ctrl+shift+i</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Display non-editable HTML page-<strong>ctrl+u</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Log in with different user-<strong>ctrl+shift+m</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5>For More advanced developer shortcuts:-</h5>\r\n<h5><a href=\"http://www.elves.in\">click here</a></h5>\r\n<h5></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"> <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Part-4</span></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">BOOKMARK</span>,<span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"> HISTORY &amp; DOWNLOADS</span></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: left;\">BOOKMARK OPERATION:-</h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Toggle (Show or hide) Bookmark bar-<strong>ctrl+shift+b</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Open Bookmark manager-<strong>ctrl+shift+o</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Save current page to your Bookmark-<strong>ctrl+b</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Save all opened tabs as a Bookmark in New folder-<strong>ctrl+shift+d</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: left;\">HISTORY OPERATION:-</h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Open the history page-<strong>ctrl+h</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Open \'clear all browsing data\' option-<strong>ctrl+shift+delete</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: left;\">DOWNLOAD OPERATION:-</h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Open download page-<strong>ctrl+j</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"> <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Part-5</span></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">ESSENTIALS</span></h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Print current page-<strong>ctrl+p</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Save the current page-<strong>ctrl+s</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Reload the page-<strong>ctrl+r</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Stop the page to load-<strong>esc</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Open a file in chrome-<strong>ctrl+o</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Toggle fullscreen-<strong>f11</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Scroll down-<strong>space</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Scroll up-<strong>shift+space</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Scroll horizontally-<strong>shift+scroll mouse wheel</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Part-6</span></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">OPERATION WITH MOUSE </span></h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">\r\n<h5>Zoom in-<strong>ctrl+wheel up</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">\r\n<h5>Zoom out-<strong>ctrl+wheel down</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">\r\n<h5>Download the target link-<strong>alt+click a link</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">\r\n<h5>Open a link in current tab-<strong>drag a link to tab</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">\r\n<h5>Open a link in New background tab-<strong>ctrl+click the link</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">\r\n<h5>Open a link in New window-<strong>shift+click the link</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5></h5>\r\n<h5></h5>', 'Useful CHROME keyboard shortcuts to speed up your productivity', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '72-autosave-v1', '', '', '2018-02-12 00:03:55', '2018-02-11 18:33:55', '', 72, 'http://techwinky.com/72-autosave-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(76, 1, '2018-01-19 01:35:12', '2018-01-18 20:05:12', 'Are you a computer geek or a employee that so spend too much time in chrome. So this article is for you. This important shortcuts will speed up of your work hence reduce anxiety and frustration.Use it and see the result.\r\n\r\n<u>Before using this shortcuts you should aware about these</u>\r\n\r\n1. Difference between TAB &amp; WINDOW.\r\n\r\n2. Chrome menu\r\n\r\n3. Bookmark manger\r\n\r\n4. Chrome task manager (For programmers and geeks)\r\n\r\n5. Find bar\r\n\r\n6. Developer tool (For programmers and geeks)\r\n\r\n7. Chrome user account\r\n\r\n8.Search bar/Address Bar\r\n<h2><b>Part-1</b></h2>\r\n<h3><b>Operation on chrome Window</b></h3>\r\n<h4>OPENING</h4>\r\nOpen a new window. <b>ctrl+n</b>\r\n\r\nOpen a new window in incognito mode. <b>ctrl+shift+n</b>\r\n\r\nOpen a new tab. <b>Ctrl+t</b>\r\n\r\nReopen previous closed tab <b>ctrl+shift+t</b>\r\n<h4>NAVIGATING THROUGH TABS</h4>\r\nJump to next open tab <b>ctrl+tab</b>\r\n\r\nJump to previous open tab <b>ctrl+shift+tab</b>\r\n\r\nGo to specify tab <b>ctrl+tab no( </b>like<b> </b>ctrl<b>+</b>1 for first tab,it will work for 1-8 only<b>)</b>\r\n\r\nGo to last tab <b>ctrl+9</b>\r\n\r\nGo back in same tab <b>alt+left arrow </b>\r\n\r\nGo forward in same tab <b>alt+right bar</b>\r\n<h4>CLOSINGS</h4>\r\nClose the current tab (Tab in which in you are working) <b>ctrl+w</b>\r\n\r\nClose the current window <b>alt+f4</b>\r\n\r\nClose browser and all open tabs <b>ctrl+shift+w</b>\r\n\r\nQuite Google chrome <b>ctrl+shift+q</b>\r\n<h4>MINIMISE</h4>\r\nMinimize the current window <b>alt+space+n</b>\r\n\r\nMaximise the already minimised window <b>alt+space+x</b>\r\n<h2>Part-2</h2>\r\n<h3><b>Smart search technique (Playing around addr</b>ess bar)</h3>\r\nSearch with a specific search engine \"search<b> engine name\"+\"search term\"+tab+enter</b>\r\n\r\nSearch with Google only. <b>\"search term\"+alt+ent</b>er\r\n\r\nAdd automatically <b>www</b> and <b>.com</b> and search store \"<b>site name\"+ctrl+enter</b>\r\n\r\nGo to search box directly and search <b>ctrl+e</b>\r\n\r\nRemove prediction from address bar. <b>\"Down arrow to highlight\" +shift+delete</b>\r\n<h2>Part-3</h2>\r\n<h3>For developers</h3>\r\nChrome menu. <b>alt+e \"or\" alt+f</b>\r\n\r\nChrome task manager <b>shift+esc</b>\r\n\r\nOpen the find bar to search the current page <b>ctrl+f</b>\r\n\r\nJump to next match in find search box <b>Ctrl+g</b>\r\n\r\nJump to previous match in find search box <b>Ctrl+shift+g</b>\r\n\r\nOpen developer tool <b>ctrl+shift+i</b>\r\n\r\nDisplay non editable HTML page <b>ctrl+u</b>\r\n\r\nLog in different user <b>ctrl+shift+m</b>\r\n<h4>For More advanced developer short cut <a href=\"elves.in\">click here</a></h4>\r\n<h2>Part-4</h2>\r\n<h3>Bookmarks,download &amp; history</h3>\r\n<h4>BOOKMARK</h4>\r\n<h4>Toggle (Show or hide) Bookmark bar <b>ctrl+shift+b</b></h4>\r\nOpen Bookmark manger <b>ctrl+shift+o</b>\r\n\r\nSave current page to your Bookmark <b>c</b><b><b>trl+b</b></b>\r\n\r\nSave all open tabs as a Bookmark in New folder <b>ctrl+shift+d</b>\r\n<h4>HISTORY</h4>\r\nOpen the history page <b>ctrl+h</b>\r\n\r\nOpen clear all browsing data option <b>Ctrl+shift+delete</b>\r\n<h4>DOWNLOAD</h4>\r\nOpen download page <b>ctrl+j</b>\r\n<h2>Part-5</h2>\r\n<h3>ESSENTIALS</h3>\r\nPrint current page <b>ctrl+p</b>\r\n\r\nSave the current page <b>ctrl+s</b>\r\n\r\nReload the page <b>ctrl+r</b>\r\n\r\nStop the page to load <b>esc</b>\r\n\r\nOpen a file in chrome <b>ctrl+o</b>\r\n\r\nToggle fullscreen <b>f11</b>\r\n\r\nScroll down <b>space</b>\r\n\r\nScroll up <b>shift+space</b>\r\n\r\nScroll horizontally <b>shift+scroll mouse wheel</b>\r\n<h2>Part-4</h2>\r\n<b>WITH MOUSE </b>\r\n\r\nzoom in <b>ctrl+wheel up </b>\r\nZoom out <b>ctrl+wheel down</b>\r\n\r\nDownload the target of link <b>alt+click a link</b>\r\n\r\nOpen a link in current tab <b>drag a link to tab</b>\r\n\r\nOpen a link in New background tab <b>ctrl+click the link</b>\r\n\r\nOpen a link in New window <b>shift+click the link</b>', 'Usefull CHROME keyboard Shortcuts to speed up your productivity', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '72-revision-v1', '', '', '2018-01-19 01:35:12', '2018-01-18 20:05:12', '', 72, 'http://techwinky.com/72-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(80, 2, '2018-01-19 15:58:35', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 'whether you are  beginner or a pro Photoshop user,this shortcuts is definitely going to speed up your work\n\n&nbsp;', 'PHOTOSHOP SHORTCUTS TO SPEED UP YOUR WORKFLOW', '', 'draft', 'open', 'open', '', '', '', '', '2018-01-19 15:58:35', '2018-01-19 10:28:35', '', 0, 'http://techwinky.com/?p=80', 0, 'post', '', 0);
INSERT INTO `wp_mtsposts` (`ID`, `post_author`, `post_date`, `post_date_gmt`, `post_content`, `post_title`, `post_excerpt`, `post_status`, `comment_status`, `ping_status`, `post_password`, `post_name`, `to_ping`, `pinged`, `post_modified`, `post_modified_gmt`, `post_content_filtered`, `post_parent`, `guid`, `menu_order`, `post_type`, `post_mime_type`, `comment_count`) VALUES
(81, 2, '2018-01-19 17:00:36', '2018-01-19 11:30:36', 'Are you a computer geek or a employee that so spend too much time in chrome. So this article is for you. This important shortcuts will speed up of your work hence reduce anxiety and frustration.Use it and see the result.\n\n<strong><u>Before using this shortcuts you should aware about these</u></strong>\n<ol>\n 	<li> Difference between TAB &amp; WINDOW.</li>\n 	<li> Chrome menu</li>\n 	<li> Bookmark manger</li>\n 	<li> Chrome task manager (For programmers and geeks)</li>\n 	<li> Find bar</li>\n 	<li> Developer tool (For programmers and geeks)</li>\n 	<li> Chrome user account</li>\n 	<li> Search bar/Address Bar</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\">PART-1</h2>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\">OPERATIONS ON WINDOW AND TABS</h3>\n<h4><strong>OPENING</strong></h4>\n<ul>\n 	<li>Open a new window. <b>ctrl+n</b></li>\n 	<li>Open a new window in incognito mode. <b>ctrl+shift+n</b></li>\n 	<li>Open a new tab. <b>Ctrl+t</b></li>\n 	<li>Reopen previous closed tab <b>ctrl+shift+t</b></li>\n</ul>\n<h4>NAVIGATING THROUGH TABS</h4>\n<ul>\n 	<li>Jump to next open tab <b>ctrl+tab</b></li>\n 	<li>Jump to previous open tab <b>ctrl+shift+tab</b></li>\n 	<li>Go to specify tab <b>ctrl+tab no( </b>like<b> </b>ctrl<b>+</b>1 for first tab,it will work for 1-8 only<b>)</b></li>\n 	<li>Go to last tab <b>ctrl+9</b></li>\n 	<li>Go back in same tab <b>alt+left arrow </b></li>\n 	<li>Go forward in same tab <b>alt+right bar</b></li>\n</ul>\n<h4>CLOSINGS</h4>\n<ul>\n 	<li>Close the current tab (Tab in which in you are working) <b>ctrl+w</b></li>\n 	<li>Close the current window <b>alt+f4</b></li>\n 	<li>Close browser and all open tabs <b>ctrl+shift+w</b></li>\n 	<li>Quite Google chrome <b>ctrl+shift+q</b></li>\n</ul>\n<h4>MINIMISE</h4>\n<ul>\n 	<li>Minimize the current window <b>alt+space+n</b></li>\n 	<li>Maximise the already minimised window <b>alt+space+x</b></li>\n</ul>\n<h2></h2>\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Part-2</strong></h2>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><b>SMART SEARCH TECHNIQUE  (Playing around addr</b>ess bar)</h3>\n<ul>\n 	<li>Search with a specific search engine \"search<b> engine name\"+\"search term\"+tab+enter</b></li>\n 	<li>Search with Google only. <b>\"search term\"+alt+ent</b>er</li>\n 	<li>Add automatically <b>www</b> and <b>.com</b> and search store \"<b>site name\"+ctrl+enter</b></li>\n 	<li>Go to search box directly and search <b>ctrl+e</b></li>\n 	<li>Remove prediction from address bar. <b>\"Down arrow to highlight\" +shift+delete</b></li>\n</ul>\n<h2></h2>\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Part-3</strong></h2>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>FOR DEVLOPERS</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n 	<li>Chrome menu. <b>alt+e \"or\" alt+f</b></li>\n 	<li>Chrome task manager <b>shift+esc</b></li>\n 	<li>Open the find bar to search the current page <b>ctrl+f</b></li>\n 	<li>Jump to next match in find search box <b>Ctrl+g</b></li>\n 	<li>Jump to previous match in find search box <b>Ctrl+shift+g</b></li>\n 	<li>Open developer tool <b>ctrl+shift+i</b></li>\n 	<li>Display non editable HTML page <b>ctrl+u</b></li>\n 	<li>Log in different user <b>ctrl+shift+m</b></li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">For More advanced developer short cut <a href=\"http://www.elves.in\">click here</a></p>\n\n<h2></h2>\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\">Part-4</h2>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>BOOKMARK</strong>,HISTORY &amp; DOWNLODS</p>\n\n<h4 style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>BOOKMARKS</strong></h4>\n<ul>\n 	<li>Toggle (Show or hide) Bookmark bar <strong>ctrl+shift+b</strong></li>\n 	<li>Open Bookmark manger <b>ctrl+shift+o</b></li>\n 	<li>Save current page to your Bookmark <b>c</b><b><b>trl+b</b></b></li>\n 	<li>Save all open tabs as a Bookmark in New folder <b>ctrl+shift+d</b></li>\n</ul>\n<h4 style=\"text-align: left;\">HISTORY</h4>\n<ul>\n 	<li>Open the history page <b>ctrl+h</b></li>\n 	<li>Open clear all browsing data option <b>Ctrl+shift+delete</b></li>\n</ul>\n<h4 style=\"text-align: left;\">DOWNLOAD</h4>\n<ul>\n 	<li>Open download page <b>ctrl+j</b></li>\n</ul>\n<h2></h2>\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\">Part-5</h2>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\">ESSENTIALS</h3>\n<ul>\n 	<li>Print current page <b>ctrl+p</b></li>\n 	<li>Save the current page <b>ctrl+s</b></li>\n 	<li>Reload the page <b>ctrl+r</b></li>\n 	<li>Stop the page to load <b>esc</b></li>\n 	<li>Open a file in chrome <b>ctrl+o</b></li>\n 	<li>Toggle fullscreen <b>f11</b></li>\n 	<li>Scroll down <b>space</b></li>\n 	<li>Scroll up <b>shift+space</b></li>\n 	<li>Scroll horizontally <b>shift+scroll mouse wheel</b></li>\n</ul>\n&nbsp;\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\">Part-4</h2>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><b>OPERATION WITH MOUSE </b></p>\n\n<ul>\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">Zoom in <b>ctrl+wheel up</b><b> </b></li>\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">Zoom out <b>ctrl+wheel down</b></li>\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">Download the target of link <b>alt+click a link</b></li>\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">Open a link in current tab <b>drag a link to tab</b></li>\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">Open a link in New background tab <b>ctrl+click the link</b></li>\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">Open a link in New window <b>shift+click the link</b></li>\n</ul>\n&nbsp;\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>QUICK AND FAST </strong></h2>\n[table id=1 /]\n\n&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;', 'Usefull CHROME keyboard Shortcuts to speed up your productivity', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '72-autosave-v1', '', '', '2018-01-19 17:00:36', '2018-01-19 11:30:36', '', 72, 'http://techwinky.com/72-autosave-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(84, 2, '2018-01-19 16:30:31', '2018-01-19 11:00:31', 'Are you a computer geek or a employee that so spend too much time in chrome. So this article is for you. This important shortcuts will speed up of your work hence reduce anxiety and frustration.Use it and see the result.\r\n\r\n<u>Before using this shortcuts you should aware about these</u>\r\n\r\n1. Difference between TAB &amp; WINDOW.\r\n\r\n2. Chrome menu\r\n\r\n3. Bookmark manger\r\n\r\n4. Chrome task manager (For programmers and geeks)\r\n\r\n5. Find bar\r\n\r\n6. Developer tool (For programmers and geeks)\r\n\r\n7. Chrome user account\r\n\r\n8.Search bar/Address Bar\r\n<h2><b>Part-1</b></h2>\r\n<h3><b>Operation on chrome Window</b></h3>\r\n<h4>OPENING</h4>\r\nOpen a new window. <b>ctrl+n</b>\r\n\r\nOpen a new window in incognito mode. <b>ctrl+shift+n</b>\r\n\r\nOpen a new tab. <b>Ctrl+t</b>\r\n\r\nReopen previous closed tab <b>ctrl+shift+t</b>\r\n<h4>NAVIGATING THROUGH TABS</h4>\r\nJump to next open tab <b>ctrl+tab</b>\r\n\r\nJump to previous open tab <b>ctrl+shift+tab</b>\r\n\r\nGo to specify tab <b>ctrl+tab no( </b>like<b> </b>ctrl<b>+</b>1 for first tab,it will work for 1-8 only<b>)</b>\r\n\r\nGo to last tab <b>ctrl+9</b>\r\n\r\nGo back in same tab <b>alt+left arrow </b>\r\n\r\nGo forward in same tab <b>alt+right bar</b>\r\n<h4>CLOSINGS</h4>\r\nClose the current tab (Tab in which in you are working) <b>ctrl+w</b>\r\n\r\nClose the current window <b>alt+f4</b>\r\n\r\nClose browser and all open tabs <b>ctrl+shift+w</b>\r\n\r\nQuite Google chrome <b>ctrl+shift+q</b>\r\n<h4>MINIMISE</h4>\r\nMinimize the current window <b>alt+space+n</b>\r\n\r\nMaximise the already minimised window <b>alt+space+x</b>\r\n<h2>Part-2</h2>\r\n<h3><b>Smart search technique (Playing around addr</b>ess bar)</h3>\r\nSearch with a specific search engine \"search<b> engine name\"+\"search term\"+tab+enter</b>\r\n\r\nSearch with Google only. <b>\"search term\"+alt+ent</b>er\r\n\r\nAdd automatically <b>www</b> and <b>.com</b> and search store \"<b>site name\"+ctrl+enter</b>\r\n\r\nGo to search box directly and search <b>ctrl+e</b>\r\n\r\nRemove prediction from address bar. <b>\"Down arrow to highlight\" +shift+delete</b>\r\n<h2>Part-3</h2>\r\n<h3>For developers</h3>\r\nChrome menu. <b>alt+e \"or\" alt+f</b>\r\n\r\nChrome task manager <b>shift+esc</b>\r\n\r\nOpen the find bar to search the current page <b>ctrl+f</b>\r\n\r\nJump to next match in find search box <b>Ctrl+g</b>\r\n\r\nJump to previous match in find search box <b>Ctrl+shift+g</b>\r\n\r\nOpen developer tool <b>ctrl+shift+i</b>\r\n\r\nDisplay non editable HTML page <b>ctrl+u</b>\r\n\r\nLog in different user <b>ctrl+shift+m</b>\r\n<h4>For More advanced developer short cut <a href=\"elves.in\">click here</a></h4>\r\n<h2>Part-4</h2>\r\n<h3>Bookmarks,download &amp; history</h3>\r\n<h4>BOOKMARK</h4>\r\n<h4>Toggle (Show or hide) Bookmark bar <b>ctrl+shift+b</b></h4>\r\nOpen Bookmark manger <b>ctrl+shift+o</b>\r\n\r\nSave current page to your Bookmark <b>c</b><b><b>trl+b</b></b>\r\n\r\nSave all open tabs as a Bookmark in New folder <b>ctrl+shift+d</b>\r\n<h4>HISTORY</h4>\r\nOpen the history page <b>ctrl+h</b>\r\n\r\nOpen clear all browsing data option <b>Ctrl+shift+delete</b>\r\n<h4>DOWNLOAD</h4>\r\nOpen download page <b>ctrl+j</b>\r\n<h2>Part-5</h2>\r\n<h3>ESSENTIALS</h3>\r\nPrint current page <b>ctrl+p</b>\r\n\r\nSave the current page <b>ctrl+s</b>\r\n\r\nReload the page <b>ctrl+r</b>\r\n\r\nStop the page to load <b>esc</b>\r\n\r\nOpen a file in chrome <b>ctrl+o</b>\r\n\r\nToggle fullscreen <b>f11</b>\r\n\r\nScroll down <b>space</b>\r\n\r\nScroll up <b>shift+space</b>\r\n\r\nScroll horizontally <b>shift+scroll mouse wheel</b>\r\n<h2>Part-4</h2>\r\n<b>WITH MOUSE </b>\r\n\r\nzoom in <b>ctrl+wheel up </b>\r\nZoom out <b>ctrl+wheel down</b>\r\n\r\nDownload the target of link <b>alt+click a link</b>\r\n\r\nOpen a link in current tab <b>drag a link to tab</b>\r\n\r\nOpen a link in New background tab <b>ctrl+click the link</b>\r\n\r\nOpen a link in New window <b>shift+click the link</b>\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>QUICK AND FAST </strong></h2>\r\n[table id=1 /]\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;', 'Usefull CHROME keyboard Shortcuts to speed up your productivity', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '72-revision-v1', '', '', '2018-01-19 16:30:31', '2018-01-19 11:00:31', '', 72, 'http://techwinky.com/72-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(86, 2, '2018-01-19 16:36:57', '2018-01-19 11:06:57', '[[\"\",\"\"],[\"\",\"\"],[\"\",\"\"],[\"\",\"\"],[\"\",\"\"],[\"\",\"\"],[\"\",\"\"],[\"\",\"\"],[\"\",\"\"],[\"\",\"\"]]', '', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', '86', '', '', '2018-01-19 16:36:57', '2018-01-19 11:06:57', '', 0, 'http://techwinky.com/?post_type=tablepress_table&p=86', 0, 'tablepress_table', 'application/json', 0),
(87, 2, '2018-01-19 16:59:27', '2018-01-19 11:29:27', 'Are you a computer geek or a employee that so spend too much time in chrome. So this article is for you. This important shortcuts will speed up of your work hence reduce anxiety and frustration.Use it and see the result.\r\n\r\n<strong><u>Before using this shortcuts you should aware about these</u></strong>\r\n<ol>\r\n 	<li> Difference between TAB &amp; WINDOW.</li>\r\n 	<li> Chrome menu</li>\r\n 	<li> Bookmark manger</li>\r\n 	<li> Chrome task manager (For programmers and geeks)</li>\r\n 	<li> Find bar</li>\r\n 	<li> Developer tool (For programmers and geeks)</li>\r\n 	<li> Chrome user account</li>\r\n 	<li> Search bar/Address Bar</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\">PART-1</h2>\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\">OPERATIONS ON WINDOW AND TABS</h3>\r\n<h4><strong>OPENING</strong></h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Open a new window. <b>ctrl+n</b></li>\r\n 	<li>Open a new window in incognito mode. <b>ctrl+shift+n</b></li>\r\n 	<li>Open a new tab. <b>Ctrl+t</b></li>\r\n 	<li>Reopen previous closed tab <b>ctrl+shift+t</b></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>NAVIGATING THROUGH TABS</h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Jump to next open tab <b>ctrl+tab</b></li>\r\n 	<li>Jump to previous open tab <b>ctrl+shift+tab</b></li>\r\n 	<li>Go to specify tab <b>ctrl+tab no( </b>like<b> </b>ctrl<b>+</b>1 for first tab,it will work for 1-8 only<b>)</b></li>\r\n 	<li>Go to last tab <b>ctrl+9</b></li>\r\n 	<li>Go back in same tab <b>alt+left arrow </b></li>\r\n 	<li>Go forward in same tab <b>alt+right bar</b></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>CLOSINGS</h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Close the current tab (Tab in which in you are working) <b>ctrl+w</b></li>\r\n 	<li>Close the current window <b>alt+f4</b></li>\r\n 	<li>Close browser and all open tabs <b>ctrl+shift+w</b></li>\r\n 	<li>Quite Google chrome <b>ctrl+shift+q</b></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>MINIMISE</h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Minimize the current window <b>alt+space+n</b></li>\r\n 	<li>Maximise the already minimised window <b>alt+space+x</b></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2></h2>\r\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Part-2</strong></h2>\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><b>SMART SEARCH TECHNIQUE  (Playing around addr</b>ess bar)</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Search with a specific search engine \"search<b> engine name\"+\"search term\"+tab+enter</b></li>\r\n 	<li>Search with Google only. <b>\"search term\"+alt+ent</b>er</li>\r\n 	<li>Add automatically <b>www</b> and <b>.com</b> and search store \"<b>site name\"+ctrl+enter</b></li>\r\n 	<li>Go to search box directly and search <b>ctrl+e</b></li>\r\n 	<li>Remove prediction from address bar. <b>\"Down arrow to highlight\" +shift+delete</b></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2></h2>\r\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Part-3</strong></h2>\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>FOR DEVLOPERS</strong></h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Chrome menu. <b>alt+e \"or\" alt+f</b></li>\r\n 	<li>Chrome task manager <b>shift+esc</b></li>\r\n 	<li>Open the find bar to search the current page <b>ctrl+f</b></li>\r\n 	<li>Jump to next match in find search box <b>Ctrl+g</b></li>\r\n 	<li>Jump to previous match in find search box <b>Ctrl+shift+g</b></li>\r\n 	<li>Open developer tool <b>ctrl+shift+i</b></li>\r\n 	<li>Display non editable HTML page <b>ctrl+u</b></li>\r\n 	<li>Log in different user <b>ctrl+shift+m</b></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">For More advanced developer short cut <a href=\"http://www.elves.in\">click here</a></p>\r\n\r\n<h2></h2>\r\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\">Part-4</h2>\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>BOOKMARK</strong>,HISTORY &amp; DOWNLODS</h3>\r\n<h4 style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>BOOKMARKS</strong></h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Toggle (Show or hide) Bookmark bar <strong>ctrl+shift+b</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Open Bookmark manger <b>ctrl+shift+o</b></li>\r\n 	<li>Save current page to your Bookmark <b>c</b><b><b>trl+b</b></b></li>\r\n 	<li>Save all open tabs as a Bookmark in New folder <b>ctrl+shift+d</b></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4 style=\"text-align: left;\">HISTORY</h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Open the history page <b>ctrl+h</b></li>\r\n 	<li>Open clear all browsing data option <b>Ctrl+shift+delete</b></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4 style=\"text-align: left;\">DOWNLOAD</h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Open download page <b>ctrl+j</b></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2></h2>\r\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\">Part-5</h2>\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\">ESSENTIALS</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Print current page <b>ctrl+p</b></li>\r\n 	<li>Save the current page <b>ctrl+s</b></li>\r\n 	<li>Reload the page <b>ctrl+r</b></li>\r\n 	<li>Stop the page to load <b>esc</b></li>\r\n 	<li>Open a file in chrome <b>ctrl+o</b></li>\r\n 	<li>Toggle fullscreen <b>f11</b></li>\r\n 	<li>Scroll down <b>space</b></li>\r\n 	<li>Scroll up <b>shift+space</b></li>\r\n 	<li>Scroll horizontally <b>shift+scroll mouse wheel</b></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\">Part-4</h2>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><b>OPERATION WITH MOUSE </b></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">Zoom in <b>ctrl+wheel up</b><b> </b></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">Zoom out <b>ctrl+wheel down</b></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">Download the target of link <b>alt+click a link</b></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">Open a link in current tab <b>drag a link to tab</b></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">Open a link in New background tab <b>ctrl+click the link</b></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">Open a link in New window <b>shift+click the link</b></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>QUICK AND FAST </strong></h2>\r\n[table id=1 /]\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;', 'Usefull CHROME keyboard Shortcuts to speed up your productivity', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '72-revision-v1', '', '', '2018-01-19 16:59:27', '2018-01-19 11:29:27', '', 72, 'http://techwinky.com/72-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
