>ctrl+wheel down</b></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">Download the target link-<b>alt+click a link</b></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">Open a link in current tab-<b>drag a link to tab</b></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">Open a link in New background tab-<b>ctrl+click the link</b></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">Open a link in New window-<b>shift+click the link</b></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\"></h2>\r\n&nbsp;', 'Useful CHROME keyboard shortcuts to speed up your productivity', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '72-revision-v1', '', '', '2018-02-11 23:40:12', '2018-02-11 18:10:12', '', 72, 'http://techwinky.com/72-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(98, 1, '2018-02-11 23:53:22', '2018-02-11 18:23:22', 'Are you a computer geek or an employee, who spend too much time using Google Chrome?\r\n\r\nThen, this article is for you. These important shortcuts will speed up of your productivity and hence, reduce anxiety and stress. Try them to see the results.\r\n\r\n<u>Before using shortcuts you should be aware of these concepts:-</u>\r\n<ol>\r\n 	<li> Difference between TAB &amp; WINDOW.</li>\r\n 	<li> Chrome menu</li>\r\n 	<li> Bookmark manager</li>\r\n 	<li> Chrome task manager (For programmers and geeks)</li>\r\n 	<li> Find bar</li>\r\n 	<li> Developer tool (For programmers and geeks)</li>\r\n 	<li> Chrome user account</li>\r\n 	<li> Search bar/Address Bar</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">PART-1</span></h3>\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">OPERATIONS ON WINDOW AND TABS</span></h3>\r\nOPEN OPERATION:-\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Open a new window- <strong>ctrl+n</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Open a new window in incognito mode- <strong>ctrl+shift+n</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Open a new tab-<strong> ctrl+t</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Reopen previously closed tab-<strong> ctrl+shift+t</strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\nNAVIGATION OPERATION:-\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Jump to next open tab-<strong>ctrl+tab</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Jump to previously open tab-<strong>ctrl+shift+tab</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Go to a specific tab- <strong>ctrl+\'tab number\'</strong> (Eg- ctrl+1 for the Ist tab.  Will work for 1-8 only)</li>\r\n 	<li>Go to last tab- <strong>ctrl+9</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Go to the previous tab from current tab- <strong>alt+left arrow</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Go to the next tab from current tab-<strong> alt+right bar</strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\nCLOSE OPERATION:-\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Close the current tab-<strong>ctrl+w</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Close the current window-<strong>alt+f4</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Close browser with all opened tabs-<strong>ctrl+shift+w</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Quite Google chrome-<strong>ctrl+shift+q</strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\nMINIMISE OPERATION:-\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Minimize the current window-<strong>alt+space+n</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Maximise the already minimized window-<strong>alt+space+x</strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"> <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Part-2</span></h3>\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">SMART SEARCH TECHNIQUE  (Playing around address bar)</span></h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Search with a specific search engine -<strong>\"search engine name\"+\"search term\"+tab+enter</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Search with Google only.- <strong>\"search term\"+alt+enter</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Add automatically www and .com in address bar- <strong>\"site name\"+ctrl+enter</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Go to address bar directly and search-<strong>ctrl+e</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Remove prediction from address bar- <strong>\"Down arrow to highlight\" +shift+delete</strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"> <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Part-3</span></h3>\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">FOR DEVELOPERS</span></h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Chrome menu-<strong>alt+e or alt+f</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Chrome task manager-<strong>shift+esc</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Open the find bar to search the current page-<strong>ctrl+f</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Jump to next match while finding-<strong>ctrl+g</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Jump to the previous match while finding-<strong>ctrl+shift+g</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Open developer tools-<strong>ctrl+shift+i</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Display non-editable HTML page-<strong>ctrl+u</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Log in with different user-<strong>ctrl+shift+m</strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\nFor More advanced developer shortcuts:-\r\n\r\n<a href=\"http://www.elves.in\">click here</a>\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"> <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Part-4</span></h3>\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">BOOKMARK</span>,<span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"> HISTORY &amp; DOWNLOADS</span></h3>\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: left;\">BOOKMARK OPERATION:-</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Toggle (Show or hide) Bookmark bar-<strong>ctrl+shift+b</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Open Bookmark manager-<strong>ctrl+shift+o</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Save current page to your Bookmark-<strong>ctrl+b</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Save all opened tabs as a Bookmark in New folder-<strong>ctrl+shift+d</strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4 style=\"text-align: left;\">HISTORY OPERATION:-</h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Open the history page-<strong>ctrl+h</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Open \'clear all browsing data\' option-<strong>ctrl+shift+delete</strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4 style=\"text-align: left;\">DOWNLOAD OPERATION:-</h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Open download page-<strong>ctrl+j</strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"> <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Part-5</span></h3>\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">ESSENTIALS</span></h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Print current page-<strong>ctrl+p</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Save the current page-<strong>ctrl+s</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Reload the page-<strong>ctrl+r</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Stop the page to load-<strong>esc</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Open a file in chrome-<strong>ctrl+o</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Toggle fullscreen-<strong>f11</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Scroll down-<strong>space</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Scroll up-<strong>shift+space</strong></li>\r\n 	<li>Scroll horizontally-<strong>shift+scroll mouse wheel</strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Part-6</span></h3>\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">OPERATION WITH MOUSE </span></h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">Zoom in-<strong>ctrl+wheel up</strong></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">Zoom out-<strong>ctrl+wheel down</strong></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">Download the target link-<strong>alt+click a link</strong></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">Open a link in current tab-<strong>drag a link to tab</strong></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">Open a link in New background tab-<strong>ctrl+click the link</strong></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">Open a link in New window-<strong>shift+click the link</strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"></p>\r\n&nbsp;', 'Useful CHROME keyboard shortcuts to speed up your productivity', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '72-revision-v1', '', '', '2018-02-11 23:53:22', '2018-02-11 18:23:22', '', 72, 'http://techwinky.com/72-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(99, 1, '2018-02-12 00:01:45', '2018-02-11 18:31:45', '<h1><img class=\"wp-image-26 alignright\" src=\"http://techwinky.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/10/IMG_20170219_110354-e1508489263874.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"183\" height=\"184\" />My Story:-</h1>\r\n<h5>Hi! I am Sanjit Chakrabarti. I am doing Btech in computer engineering, graduating in 2019.</h5>\r\n<h5>After learning to code in my second semester, I started using only Linux in 2016. I started with Ubuntu first, as usual. I then finished reading this Book \'<a href=\"http://linuxcommand.org/tlcl.php\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Linux Command Line</a>\' and did a course on Linux administration in Udemy (LINK:- <a href=\"https://www.udemy.com/linux-administration/learn/v4/\">https://www.udemy.com/linux-administration/learn/v4/</a> ).</h5>\r\n<h5>Then after tinkering with Ubuntu for months, I installed Arch Linux on my PC to get more control over my OS. I am now a happy user of Arch Linux. So, I opened this blog to share some great tips and tutorials on Arch Linux. Hope to make Arch Linux as simple as possible.</h5>\r\n<h5>I am also an Android developer.</h5>\r\n<h5>In free time, I like to cycle far away places.</h5>\r\n<h5></h5>\r\n<h5>Follow me on:-</h5>\r\n<h5>Twitter - <a href=\"https://twitter.com/sujitsanjit?lang=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">@sujitsanjit</a></h5>\r\n<h5>Linkedin - <a href=\"http://www.linkedin.com/in/sanjit-chakrabarti-pro\">sanjit-chakrabarti-pro</a></h5>\r\n<h5>Check out my work -  <a href=\"https://github.com/sanjitchak\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">sanjitchak</a></h5>', 'About Me', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '24-revision-v1', '', '', '2018-02-12 00:01:45', '2018-02-11 18:31:45', '', 24, 'http://techwinky.com/24-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(100, 1, '2018-02-12 00:03:08', '2018-02-11 18:33:08', '<h1><img class=\"wp-image-26 alignright\" src=\"http://techwinky.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/10/IMG_20170219_110354-e1508489263874.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"183\" height=\"184\" />My Story:-</h1>\r\n<h5>Hi! I am Sanjit Chakrabarti. I am doing Btech in computer engineering, graduating in 2019.</h5>\r\n<h5>After learning to code in my second semester, I started using only Linux in 2016. I started with Ubuntu first, as usual. I then finished reading this Book \'<a href=\"http://linuxcommand.org/tlcl.php\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Linux Command Line</a>\' and did a course on Linux administration in Udemy (LINK:- <a href=\"https://www.udemy.com/linux-administration/learn/v4/\">https://www.udemy.com/linux-administration/learn/v4/</a> ).</h5>\r\n<h5>Then after tinkering with Ubuntu for months, I installed Arch Linux on my PC to get more control over my OS. I am now a happy user of Arch Linux. So, I opened this blog to share some great tips and tutorials on Arch Linux. Hope to make Arch Linux as simple as possible.</h5>\r\n<h5>I am also on my way to become a full-time Android developer too.</h5>\r\n<h5>In free time, I like to cycle far away places.</h5>\r\n<h5></h5>\r\n<h5>Follow me on:-</h5>\r\n<h5>Twitter - <a href=\"https://twitter.com/sujitsanjit?lang=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">@sujitsanjit</a></h5>\r\n<h5>Linkedin - <a href=\"http://www.linkedin.com/in/sanjit-chakrabarti-pro\">sanjit-chakrabarti-pro</a></h5>\r\n<h5>Check out my work -  <a href=\"https://github.com/sanjitchak\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">sanjitchak</a></h5>', 'About Me', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '24-revision-v1', '', '', '2018-02-12 00:03:08', '2018-02-11 18:33:08', '', 24, 'http://techwinky.com/24-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0);
INSERT INTO `wp_mtsposts` (`ID`, `post_author`, `post_date`, `post_date_gmt`, `post_content`, `post_title`, `post_excerpt`, `post_status`, `comment_status`, `ping_status`, `post_password`, `post_name`, `to_ping`, `pinged`, `post_modified`, `post_modified_gmt`, `post_content_filtered`, `post_parent`, `guid`, `menu_order`, `post_type`, `post_mime_type`, `comment_count`) VALUES
(101, 1, '2018-02-12 00:04:09', '2018-02-11 18:34:09', '<h5>Are you a computer geek or an employee, who spend too much time using Google Chrome?</h5>\r\n<h5>Then, this article is for you. These important shortcuts will speed up of your productivity and hence, reduce anxiety and stress. Try them to see the results.</h5>\r\n<h5><u>Before using shortcuts you should be aware of these concepts:-</u></h5>\r\n<ol>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5> Difference between TAB &amp; WINDOW.</h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5> Chrome menu</h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5> Bookmark manager</h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5> Chrome task manager (For programmers and geeks)</h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5> Find bar</h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5> Developer tool (For programmers and geeks)</h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5> Chrome user account</h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5> Search bar/Address Bar</h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<h5></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">PART-1</span></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">OPERATIONS ON WINDOW AND TABS</span></h5>\r\n<h5>OPEN OPERATION:-</h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Open a new window- <strong>ctrl+n</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Open a new window in incognito mode- <strong>ctrl+shift+n</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Open a new tab-<strong> ctrl+t</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Reopen previously closed tab-<strong> ctrl+shift+t</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5>NAVIGATION OPERATION:-</h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Jump to next open tab-<strong>ctrl+tab</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Jump to previously open tab-<strong>ctrl+shift+tab</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Go to a specific tab- <strong>ctrl+\'tab number\'</strong> (Eg- ctrl+1 for the Ist tab.  Will work for 1-8 only)</h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Go to last tab- <strong>ctrl+9</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Go to the previous tab from current tab- <strong>alt+left arrow</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Go to the next tab from current tab-<strong> alt+right bar</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5>CLOSE OPERATION:-</h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Close the current tab-<strong>ctrl+w</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Close the current window-<strong>alt+f4</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Close browser with all opened tabs-<strong>ctrl+shift+w</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Quite Google chrome-<strong>ctrl+shift+q</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5>MINIMISE OPERATION:-</h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Minimize the current window-<strong>alt+space+n</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Maximise the already minimized window-<strong>alt+space+x</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"> <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Part-2</span></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">SMART SEARCH TECHNIQUE  (Playing around address bar)</span></h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Search with a specific search engine -<strong>\"search engine name\"+\"search term\"+tab+enter</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Search with Google only.- <strong>\"search term\"+alt+enter</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Add automatically www and .com in address bar- <strong>\"site name\"+ctrl+enter</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Go to address bar directly and search-<strong>ctrl+e</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Remove prediction from address bar- <strong>\"Down arrow to highlight\" +shift+delete</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"> <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Part-3</span></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">FOR DEVELOPERS</span></h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Chrome menu-<strong>alt+e or alt+f</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Chrome task manager-<strong>shift+esc</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Open the find bar to search the current page-<strong>ctrl+f</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Jump to next match while finding-<strong>ctrl+g</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Jump to the previous match while finding-<strong>ctrl+shift+g</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Open developer tools-<strong>ctrl+shift+i</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Display non-editable HTML page-<strong>ctrl+u</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Log in with different user-<strong>ctrl+shift+m</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5>For More advanced developer shortcuts:-</h5>\r\n<h5><a href=\"http://www.elves.in\">click here</a></h5>\r\n<h5></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"> <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Part-4</span></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">BOOKMARK</span>,<span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"> HISTORY &amp; DOWNLOADS</span></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: left;\">BOOKMARK OPERATION:-</h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Toggle (Show or hide) Bookmark bar-<strong>ctrl+shift+b</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Open Bookmark manager-<strong>ctrl+shift+o</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Save current page to your Bookmark-<strong>ctrl+b</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Save all opened tabs as a Bookmark in New folder-<strong>ctrl+shift+d</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: left;\">HISTORY OPERATION:-</h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Open the history page-<strong>ctrl+h</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Open \'clear all browsing data\' option-<strong>ctrl+shift+delete</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: left;\">DOWNLOAD OPERATION:-</h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Open download page-<strong>ctrl+j</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"> <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Part-5</span></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">ESSENTIALS</span></h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Print current page-<strong>ctrl+p</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Save the current page-<strong>ctrl+s</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Reload the page-<strong>ctrl+r</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Stop the page to load-<strong>esc</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Open a file in chrome-<strong>ctrl+o</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Toggle fullscreen-<strong>f11</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Scroll down-<strong>space</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Scroll up-<strong>shift+space</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li>\r\n<h5>Scroll horizontally-<strong>shift+scroll mouse wheel</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Part-6</span></h5>\r\n<h5 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">OPERATION WITH MOUSE </span></h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">\r\n<h5>Zoom in-<strong>ctrl+wheel up</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">\r\n<h5>Zoom out-<strong>ctrl+wheel down</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">\r\n<h5>Download the target link-<strong>alt+click a link</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">\r\n<h5>Open a link in current tab-<strong>drag a link to tab</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">\r\n<h5>Open a link in New background tab-<strong>ctrl+click the link</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n 	<li style=\"text-align: left;\">\r\n<h5>Open a link in New window-<strong>shift+click the link</strong></h5>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5></h5>\r\n<h5></h5>', 'Useful CHROME keyboard shortcuts to speed up your productivity', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '72-revision-v1', '', '', '2018-02-12 00:04:09', '2018-02-11 18:34:09', '', 72, 'http://techwinky.com/72-revision-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(104, 1, '2018-03-30 21:57:41', '2018-03-30 16:27:41', '<div id=\"ppBody\">\r\n<div class=\"grayText\"><strong>What personal information do we collect from the people that visit our blog, website or app?</strong></div>\r\n<div class=\"innerText\">When ordering or registering on our app, as appropriate, you may be asked to enter your name, email address, phone number or other details to help you with your experience.</div>\r\n<div class=\"grayText\"><strong>When do we collect information?</strong></div>\r\n<div class=\"innerText\">We collect information from you when you fill out a form or enter information on our app.</div>\r\n<span id=\"infoUs\"></span>\r\n<div class=\"grayText\"><strong>How do we use your information?</strong></div>\r\n<div class=\"innerText\">We may use the information we collect from you when you register, make a purchase, sign up for our newsletter, respond to a survey or marketing communication, surf the website, or use certain other site features in the following ways:\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"innerText\">      <strong>•</strong> To personalize your experience and to allow us to deliver the type of content and product offerings in which you are most interested.</div>\r\n<span id=\"infoPro\"></span>\r\n<div class=\"grayText\"><strong>How do we protect your information?</strong></div>\r\n<div class=\"innerText\">We do not use vulnerability scanning and/or scanning to PCI standards.</div>\r\n<div class=\"innerText\">We only provide articles and information. We never ask for credit card numbers.</div>\r\n<div class=\"innerText\">We do not use Malware Scanning.\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"innerText\">We do not use an SSL certificate</div>\r\n<div class=\"innerText\">      <strong>•</strong> We do not need an SSL because:</div>\r\n<div class=\"innerText\">Information is not transmitted</div>\r\n<span id=\"coUs\"></span>\r\n<div class=\"grayText\"><strong>Do we use \'cookies\'?</strong></div>\r\n<div class=\"innerText\">We do not use cookies for tracking purposes</div>\r\n<div class=\"innerText\">\r\nYou can choose to have your computer warn you each time a cookie is being sent, or you can choose to turn off all cookies. You do this through your browser settings. Since browser is a little different, look at your browser\'s Help Menu to learn the correct way to modify your cookies.</div>\r\n<div class=\"innerText\">If you turn cookies off, Some of the features that make your site experience more efficient may not function properly.that make your site experience more efficient and may not function properly.</div>\r\n<span id=\"trDi\"></span>\r\n<div class=\"grayText\"><strong>Third-party disclosure</strong></div>\r\n<div class=\"innerText\">We do not sell, trade, or otherwise transfer to outside parties your Personally Identifiable Information.</div>\r\n<span id=\"trLi\"></span>\r\n<div class=\"grayText\"><strong>Third-party links</strong></div>\r\n<div class=\"innerText\">We do not include or offer third-party products or services on our website.</div>\r\n<span id=\"gooAd\"></span>\r\n<div class=\"blueText\"><strong>Google</strong></div>\r\n<div class=\"innerText\">Google\'s advertising requirements can be summed up by Google\'s Advertising Principles. They are put in place to provide a positive experience for users. https://support.google.com/adwordspolicy/answer/1316548?hl=en\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"innerText\">We have not enabled Google AdSense on our site but we may do so in the future.</div>\r\n<div class=\"innerText\">app</div>\r\n<span id=\"coppAct\"></span>\r\n<div class=\"blueText\"><strong>COPPA (Children Online Privacy Protection Act)</strong></div>\r\n<div class=\"innerText\">When it comes to the collection of personal information from children under the age of 13 years old, the Children\'s Online Privacy Protection Act (COPPA) puts parents in control. The Federal Trade Commission, United States\' consumer protection agency, enforces the COPPA Rule, which spells out what operators of websites and online services must do to protect children\'s privacy and safety online.\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"innerText\">We do not specifically market to children under the age of 13 years old.</div>\r\n<div class=\"innerText\">Do we let third-parties, including ad networks or plug-ins collect PII from children under 13?</div>\r\n<span id=\"ftcFip\"></span>\r\n<div class=\"blueText\"><strong>Fair Information Practices</strong></div>\r\n<div class=\"innerText\">The Fair Information Practices Principles form the backbone of privacy law in the United States and the concepts they include have played a significant role in the development of data protection laws around the globe. Understanding the Fair Information Practice Principles and how they should be implemented is critical to comply with the various privacy laws that protect personal information.\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<span id=\"canSpam\"></span></div>\r\n<span id=\"ourCon\"></span>\r\n<div class=\"blueText\"><strong>Contacting Us</strong></div>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<div class=\"innerText\">If there are any questions regarding this privacy policy, you may contact us using the information below.\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"innerText\">http://techwinky.com</div>', 'Privacy Policy of App', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'privacy-policy-app', '', '', '2018-03-30 21:57:41', '2018-03-30 16:27:41', '', 0, 'http://techwinky.com/?page_id=104', 0, 'page', '', 0),
